down","id":"38cd1bd7","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.046049,"end_time":"2026-06-22T22:38:02.516944","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-06-22T22:38:02.470895","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["# 8. IHT vs Universal Credit households\n","\n","This section adds Universal Credit data to the LAD-level IHT analysis.\n","\n","The Universal Credit file is at Output Area (OA) level, so it is first aggregated to Local Authority District (LAD) level using lad_code. After that, the LAD-level UC totals are joined to lad_iht_estimates so the relationship between IHT and UC can be compared at the same geographic level.\n","\n","This measures **households on Universal Credit**, not individual claimants. \n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"71d87520","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.049082,"end_time":"2026-06-22T22:38:02.611601","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-06-22T22:38:02.562519","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["Flow chart for this added section:\n","\n","1. Load Universal Credit OA-level data\n","\n","2. Clean UC variables\n","\n","3. Aggregate UC data from OA → LAD\n","\n","4. Create full LAD population table (from lookup + LSOA population)\n","\n","5. Join: IHT LAD estimates + full LAD population + UC LAD table\n","\n","6. Create analysis variables:\n","- IHT value per capita\n","- IHT estates per 10k\n","- UC households per 10k\n","- log versions\n","  \n","7. Check join coverage and denominator quality\n","  \n","8. Run correlations\n"," \n","9. Plot relationships:\n","- IHT vs UC\n","- log IHT vs log UC\n","- log IHT vs log UC (minus zero IHT values)\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":43,"id":"40cf1f05","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-06-22T22:38:02.704299Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-06-22T22:38:02.702401Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-06-22T22:38:03.425171Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-06-22T22:38:03.42249Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.774218,"end_time":"2026-06-22T22:38:03.428972","exception":false,"start_tim